122. GLUTEN-FREE LIVING
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Category : K · Lifestyle & Goal-Based Nutrition
Focus    : Everyday eating built on naturally gluten-free whole foods — rice, yam, plantain, potatoes, beans, maize, fish, meat, fruit & vegetables — with no wheat, barley or rye.
Best for : People who feel better off gluten, or choose gluten-free; naturally suits most Nigerian/West-African staples.
Caution  : Gluten-free is medically NECESSARY only for coeliac disease or gluten sensitivity — for others it isn't proven healthier and can lower fibre/B-vitamins unless built on whole foods. Suspect coeliac? Get tested BEFORE cutting gluten. Watch label & oat cross-contamination.
Targets  : ~2000 kcal · No wheat/barley/rye · Whole naturally-GF foods · Fibre 30g+
